        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: guard generated video downloads [AI]",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users generating videos from providers that return URL-only assets could have the CLI download provider-supplied URLs without applying the configured provider request network policy.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe CLI now resolves the selected provider's request policy for URL-only generated video assets and downloads them through the guarded provider HTTP path. This preserves streaming output and in-memory size caps while keeping provider request config as the opt-in path for private-network downloads.\n\n## User Impact\n\nCLI video generation keeps working for normal provider-hosted media, blocks private/internal download targets by default, and still permits configured private-network providers when operators opt into that request policy.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- AI-assisted.\n- `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/cli/capability-cli.test.ts` passed: 108 tests.\n- `git diff --check origin/main...HEAD` passed.\n- `corepack pnpm exec oxfmt --check --threads=1 src/cli/capability-cli.ts src/cli/capability-cli.test.ts` passed.\n- Remote Testbox/Crabbox proof unavailable: the wrapper sanity check failed because no usable `crabbox` binary was available in this worktree.\n",
